    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d240-a3">

                <pb facs="0227" n="905" sameAs="frus:frus1863p2/pg905"/>


                <head>Wansiang, Tung, and Pankiene to Mr. Burlingame</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1862-08-23"><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >August</hi> 23, 1862.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p>Your note, with the accompanying copy of the History of the United States, has
                    been received. I shall most carefully look the work over, and, therefore, be
                    able to obtain a thorough knowledge of the customs, the geography, and the
                    character of the people of that country. I shall keep the volume at my side, and
                    be gradually extending my information as I look at it.</p>
                <p>I return this note of thanks for it, at the same time availing myself of the
                    opportunity to wish you happiness.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>Cards of WANSIANG, TUNG, and PANKIENE.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
